<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL-PepsiCo up 1-1/4 to 31-1/2.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL-PepsiCo up 1-1/4 to 31-1/2.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of PepsiCo Inc rose 1-1/4 to 31-1/2 in light volume, traders said.</p>
<p>After the market closed, PepsiCo said it will restructure its international operations and review its casual dining businesses.  </p>
<p>Trading activity was otherwise light, traders said.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said that Keithley Instruments Inc, Coleman Co Inc, A.H. Belo Corp and Providence Journal Co were unavailable for after hours trade.</p>
<p>The NYSE said session one volume was 32,800 shares, compared to 17,600 shares Wednesday. Session two volume was 985,900 versus 25,186,356.</p>
<p>The American Stock Exchange said there was no after-hours activity.</p>
<p>--S. Spielberg 212 859-1700</p>
</text>
